menu "Headset: power (modules/hs_power)"

    config HS_POWER_LOW_PERCENT
        int "Low-battery warning at or below (%)"
        default 10
        range 1 50

    config HS_POWER_CRITICAL_MV
        int "Power off on battery at or below (mV)"
        default 3400
        range 3000 3700
        help
            Above the BQ24074's and the cell's own protection, so the headset
            switches itself off cleanly (audio muted, LED shown) before brown-out
            does it noisily. The TPS63001 buck-boost holds 3.3 V well below this.

    config HS_POWER_FULL_MV
        int "With external power, treat the cell as full at or above (mV)"
        default 4150
        range 4000 4200
        help
            The charger's status pin is not wired to the S3 on ORGA v1 (TBD-015),
            so "charged" is inferred from voltage while power is good.

    config HS_POWER_RELEASE_WAIT_MS
        int "Wait at most this long for the power button's release (ms)"
        default 10000
        range 0 60000
        help
            The power button also holds the regulator on, so power cannot drop
            until it is released.

    config HS_POWER_AUTO_OFF_MIN
        int "Power off after this long not worn, on battery (min); 0 = never"
        default 15
        range 0 600
        help
            "Not worn" is the IMU reporting stillness (modules/hs_sense). With
            external power the headset never switches itself off.

endmenu
